(489,1100,'A chronic communicable infection which is a principal or polar form of LEPROSY. This disorder is caused by MYCOBACTERIUM LEPRAE and produces diffuse granulomatous skin lesions in the form of nodules, macules, or papules. The peripheral nerves are involved symmetrically and neural sequelae occur in the advanced stage.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:03',NULL,NULL,'11004FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(490,1101,'Motor behavior that is repetitive, often seemingly driven, and nonfunctional. This behavior markedly interferes with normal activities or results in severe bodily self-injury. The behavior is not due to the direct physiological effects of a substance or a general medical condition. (DSM-IV, 1994)','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:03',NULL,NULL,'7723FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
