(760,1562,'Cognitive disorders including delirium, dementia, and other cognitive disorders. These may be the result of substance use, trauma, or other causes.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:11',NULL,NULL,'5640FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(761,1564,'An acute infectious disease of the central nervous system affecting almost all mammals, including humans. It is caused by a rhabdovirus and usually spread by contamination with virus-laden saliva of bites inflicted by rabid animals. Important animal vectors include the dog, cat, vampire bat, mongoose, skunk, wolf, raccoon, and fox. (From Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:11',NULL,NULL,'7079FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(762,1566,'A general term for the complete or partial loss of the ability to hear from one or both ears. Deafness may result from EAR DISEASES; VESTIBULOCOCHLEAR NERVE DISEASES; or BRAIN DISEASES.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:11',NULL,NULL,'13688FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
