(885,1822,'A hair-containing cyst or sinus, occurring chiefly in the coccygeal region.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:16',NULL,NULL,'13382FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(886,1823,'A syndrome produced by severe protein deficiency, characterized by retarded growth, changes in skin and hair pigment, edema, and pathologic changes in the liver, including fatty infiltration, necrosis, and fibrosis. The word is a local name in Gold Coast, Africa, meaning &quot;displaced child&quot;. Although first reported from Africa, kwashiorkor is now known throughout the world, but mainly in the tropics and subtropics. It is considered to be related to marasmus. (From Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:16',NULL,NULL,'5782FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(887,1826,'A nutritional condition produced by a deficiency of VITAMIN A in the diet, characterized by NIGHT BLINDNESS and other ocular manifestations such as dryness of the conjunctiva and later of the cornea (XEROPHTHALMIA). Vitamin A deficiency is a very common problem worldwide, particularly in developing countries as a consequence of famine or shortages of vitamin A-rich foods. In the United States it is found among the urban poor, the elderly, alcoholics, and patients with malabsorption. (From Cecil Textbook of Medicine, 19th ed, p1179)','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:16',NULL,NULL,'6894FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(888,1827,'A collective term for muscle and ligament injuries without dislocation or fracture. A sprain is a joint injury in which some of the fibers of a supporting ligament are ruptured but the continuity of the ligament remains intact. A strain is an overstretching or overexertion of some part of the musculature.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:16',NULL,NULL,'3426FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(889,1828,'Symmetrical osteitis of the four limbs, chiefly localized to the phalanges and the terminal epiphyses of the long bones of the forearm and leg, sometimes extending to the proximal ends of the limbs and the flat bones, and accompanied by dorsal kyphosis and joint involvement. It is often secondary to chronic conditions of the lungs and heart. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:16',NULL,NULL,'4757FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(890,1831,'Cause of death of the child','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:16',NULL,NULL,'16117FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(891,1832,'Dryness of the eye surfaces caused by deficiency of tears or conjunctival secretions. It may be associated with vitamin A deficiency, trauma, or any condition in which the eyelids do not close completely.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:16',NULL,NULL,'6888FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(892,1833,'Disorders in which anxiety (persistent feelings of apprehension, tension, or uneasiness) is the predominant disturbance.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:16',NULL,NULL,'15059FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(893,1835,'A collective term for muscle and ligament injuries without dislocation or fracture. A sprain is a joint injury in which some of the fibers of a supporting ligament are ruptured but the continuity of the ligament remains intact. A strain is an overstretching or overexertion of some part of the musculature.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:16',NULL,NULL,'7452FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(894,1836,'Disorders in which anxiety (persistent feelings of apprehension, tension, or uneasiness) is the predominant disturbance.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:16',NULL,NULL,'15057FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(895,1840,'A true cyst of the pancreas to be distinguished from the much more common PANCREATIC PSEUDOCYST by possessing a mucous epithelial lining. Pancreatic cysts are categorized as congenital, retention, neoplastic, parasitic, enterogenous, or dermoid. Congenital cysts occur more frequently as solitary cysts but may be multiple. Retention cysts are gross enlargements of pancreatic ducts secondary to ductal obstruction. (From Bockus Gastroenterology, 4th ed, p4145)','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:16',NULL,NULL,'13377FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(896,1841,'Abnormal enlargement or overgrowth of the gingivae brought about by enlargement of existing cells.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:16',NULL,NULL,'3968FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(897,1842,'A localized infection of mucous membranes or skin caused by toxigenic strains of CORYNEBACTERIUM DIPHTHERIAE. It is characterized by the presence of a pseudomembrane at the site of infection. DIPHTHERIA TOXIN, produced by C. diphtheriae, can cause myocarditis, polyneuritis, and other systemic toxic effects.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:16',NULL,NULL,'5682FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(898,1843,'A repetitive and persistent pattern of behavior in which the basic rights of others or major age-appropriate societal norms or rules are violated. These behaviors include aggressive conduct that causes or threatens physical harm to other people or animals, nonagressive conduct that causes property loss or damage, deceitfulness or theft, and serious violations of rules. The onset is before age 18. (From DSM-IV, 1994)','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:16',NULL,NULL,'5541FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(899,1844,'Calculi occurring in the kidney. Calculi too large to pass spontaneously range in size from 1 cm to the staghorn stones that occupy the renal pelvis and calyces.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:16',NULL,NULL,'4753FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(900,1846,'An acute form of TUBERCULOSIS in which minute tubercles are formed in a number of organs of the body due to dissemination of the bacilli through the blood stream.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:16',NULL,NULL,'5535FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(901,1847,'A disease of infants due to group 2 phage type 17 staphylococci that produce an epidermolytic exotoxin. Superficial fine vesicles and bullae form and rupture easily, resulting in loss of large sheets of epidermis.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:17',NULL,NULL,'3417FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(902,1849,'State in which an individual perceives or experiences a sensation of unreality concerning the self or the environment; it is seen in disorders such as schizophrenia, affection disorders, organic mental disorders, and personality disorders. (APA, Thesaurus of Psychological Index Terms, 8th ed.)','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:17',NULL,NULL,'5528FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(903,1851,'Conditions in which increased pressure within a limited space compromises the circulation and function of tissue within that space. Compartmentation involves mainly the leg but also involved are the forearm, arm, thigh, shoulder, and buttock. Some of the causes of increased pressure are trauma, tight dressings, hemorrhage, and exercise. Sequelae include nerve compression, paralysis, and contracture.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:17',NULL,NULL,'3959FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(904,1853,'Backflow of blood from the aorta into the left ventricle, owing to imperfect functioning of the aortic semilunar valve.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:17',NULL,NULL,'15051FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(905,1856,'Localized destruction of the tooth surface initiated by decalcification of the enamel followed by enzymatic lysis of organic structures and leading to cavity formation. If left unchecked, the cavity may penetrate the enamel and dentin and reach the pulp. The three most prominent theories used to explain the etiology of the disase are that acids produced by bacteria lead to decalcification; that micro-organisms destroy the enamel protein; or that keratolytic micro-organisms produce chelates that lead to decalcification.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:17',NULL,NULL,'6188FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(906,1859,'Infections or infestations with parasitic organisms. They are often contracted through contact with an intermediate vector, but may occur as the result of direct exposure.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:17',NULL,NULL,'5676FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(907,1860,'Increased intracellular or extracellular fluid in brain tissue. Cytotoxic brain edema (swelling due to increased intracellular fluid) is indicative of a disturbance in cell metabolism, and is commonly associated with hypoxic or ischemic injuries (see HYPOXIA, BRAIN). An increase in extracellular fluid may be caused by increased brain capillary permeability (vasogenic edema), an osmotic gradient, local blockages in interstitial fluid pathways, or by obstruction of CSF flow (e.g., obstructive HYDROCEPHALUS). (From Childs Nerv Syst 1992 Sep; 8(6):301-6)','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:17',NULL,NULL,'6174FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
