(910,1865,'General or unspecified injuries to the chest area.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:17',NULL,NULL,'6153FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(911,1867,'Increase in the mass of bone per unit volume.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:17',NULL,NULL,'4730FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(912,1871,'General or unspecified diseases of the blood vessels outside the heart. It is for diseases of the peripheral as opposed to the cardiac circulation.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:17',NULL,NULL,'3957FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(913,1874,'Chest pain of cardiac origin.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:17',NULL,NULL,'15987FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(914,1875,'Infection with CYTOMEGALOVIRUS, characterized by enlarged cells bearing intranuclear inclusions. Infection may be in almost any organ, but the salivary glands are the most common site in children, as are the lungs in adults.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:17',NULL,NULL,'13365FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(915,1878,'Acute, localized autoinoculable infectious disease usually acquired through sexual contact. Caused by HAEMOPHILUS DUCREYI, it occurs endemically almost worldwide, especially in tropical and subtropical countries and more commonly in seaports and urban areas than in rural areas.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:17',NULL,NULL,'14187FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(916,1879,'Skin diseases characterized by local or general distributions of blisters. They are classified according to the site and mode of blister formation. Lesions can appear spontaneously or be precipitated by infection, trauma, or sunlight. Etiologies include immunologic and genetic factors. (From Scientific American Medicine, 1990)','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:17',NULL,NULL,'3378FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
