(935,1916,'An inflammatory disease of the liver caused by hepatitis C virus lasting six months or more.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:18',NULL,NULL,'14037FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(936,1918,'Chronically depressed mood that occurs for most of the day more days than not for at least 2 years. The required minimum duration in children to make this diagnosis is 1 year. During periods of depressed mood, at least 2 of the following additional symptoms are present: poor appetite or overeating, insomnia or hypersomnia, low energy or fatigue, low self esteem, poor concentration or difficulty making decisions, and feelings of hopelessness. (DSM-IV)','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:18',NULL,NULL,'5488FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(937,1920,'General or unspecified injuries involving the fingers.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:18',NULL,NULL,'15538FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(938,1924,'A distinct and virulent form of DENGUE characterized by thrombocytopenia and hemoconcentration (grades I and II) and distinguished by a positive tourniquet test. When accompanied by circulatory failure and shock (grades III and IV), it is called dengue shock syndrome. (From Dorland, 28th ed)','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:18',NULL,NULL,'13287FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(939,1926,'Leukemia associated with hyperplasia and overactivity of the lymphoid tissue. There are increased numbers of circulating malignant lymphocytes and lymphoblasts. (Dorland, 28th ed, p919)','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:18',NULL,NULL,'4660FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(940,1927,'A chronic endemic form of hypoplasia of the dental enamel caused by drinking water with a high fluorine content during the time of tooth formation, and characterized by defective calcification that gives a white chalky appearance to the enamel, which gradually undergoes brown discoloration. (Jablonski&#39;s Dictionary of Dentistry, 1992, p286)','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:18',NULL,NULL,'13282FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
