(1113,2264,'The prolapse of one part of the intestine into the lumen of an immediately adjoining part. There are four varieties: colic, involving segments of the large intestine; enteric, involving only the small intestine; ileocecal, in which the ileocecal valve prolapses into the cecum, drawing the ileum along with it; and ileocolic, in which the ileum prolapses through the ileocecal valve into the colon. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:24',NULL,NULL,'11214FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
