(1402,2880,'An inflammatory, pruritic disease of the skin and mucous membranes, which can be either generalized or localized. It is characterized by distinctive purplish, flat-topped papules having a predilection for the trunk and flexor surfaces. The lesions may be discrete or coalesce to form plaques. Histologically, there is a &quot;saw-tooth&quot; pattern of epidermal hyperplasia and vacuolar alteration of the basal layer of the epidermis along with an intense upper dermal inflammatory infiltrate composed predominantly of T-cells. Etiology is unknown.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:35',NULL,NULL,'10963FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
