(1408,2887,'Infection with CYSTICERCUS, a larval form of the various tapeworms of the genus Taenia (usually T. solium in man). In humans they penetrate the intestinal wall and invade subcutaneous tissue, brain, eye, muscle, heart, liver, lung, and peritoneum. Brain involvement results in NEUROCYSTICERCOSIS. (From Dorland, 28th ed)','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:35',NULL,NULL,'11403FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1409,2888,'A fulminating group A streptococcal infection beginning with severe or extensive cellulitis that spreads to involve the superficial and deep fascia, producing thrombosis of the subcutaneous vessels and gangrene of the underlying tissues. A cutaneous lesion usually serves as a portal of entry for the infection, but sometimes no such lesion is found. (Dorland, 28th ed)','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:35',NULL,NULL,'10017FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1410,2889,'An inflammatory, pruritic disease of the skin and mucous membranes, which can be either generalized or localized. It is characterized by distinctive purplish, flat-topped papules having a predilection for the trunk and flexor surfaces. The lesions may be discrete or coalesce to form plaques. Histologically, there is a &quot;saw-tooth&quot; pattern of epidermal hyperplasia and vacuolar alteration of the basal layer of the epidermis along with an intense upper dermal inflammatory infiltrate composed predominantly of T-cells. Etiology is unknown.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:35',NULL,NULL,'10962FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1411,2892,'Epileptic seizure of unspecified type.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:35',NULL,NULL,'207FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1412,2894,'An extremely variable eczematous skin disease that is presumed to be a response to prolonged vigorous scratching, rubbing, or pinching to relieve intense pruritus. It varies in intensity, severity, course, and morphologic expression in different individuals. Neurodermatitis is believed by some to be psychogenic. The circumscribed or localized form is often referred to as lichen simplex chronicus.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:35',NULL,NULL,'10961FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1413,2896,'Anemia, due to the destruction or dissolution of red blood cells, with subsequent release of hemoglobin.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:35',NULL,NULL,'2FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1414,2896,'Ø®ÙˆÙ† Ú©Û’ Ø³Ø±Ø® Ø°Ø±Ø§Øª Ù¹ÙˆÙ¹Ù†Û’ Ú©Û’ Ø¨Ø¹Ø¯ ÛÛŒÙ…ÙˆÚ©Ù„ÙˆØ¨Ù† Ø¨Ø§ÛØ± Ù†Ú©Ù„Ù†Û’ Ú©ÛŒ ÙˆØ¬Û Ø³Û’ Ø®ÙˆÙ† Ú©ÛŒ Ú©Ù…ÛŒ','ur',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:35',NULL,NULL,'18133FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1415,2901,'Group of chronic blistering diseases characterized histologically by acantholysis and blister formation within the epidermis.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:35',NULL,NULL,'9281FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1416,2906,'An inflammatory process involving the chorion, its fetal blood vessels, the umbilical cord, and the amnion by extension of the inflammation, as the amnion itself has no blood supply. This inflammatory process is potentially fatal to mother and fetus.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:35',NULL,NULL,'11370FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1417,2907,'A chronic, localized hardening and thickening of the skin. Lesions may be categorized as morphea (guttate, profunda, pansclerotic) or linear (with or without melorheostosis or hemiatrophy). It is twice as common in women as in men. The condition is characterized by skin ischemia, lymphocytic infiltrates, swollen collagen bundles, and thickening of the dermis with reduction of subcutaneous fat.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:35',NULL,NULL,'10953FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
