(1446,2964,'Loss of the ability to maintain awareness of self and environment combined with markedly reduced responsiveness to environmental stimuli. (From Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, pp344-5)','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:36',NULL,NULL,'10904FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1447,2965,'Absence of hair from areas where it is normally present.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:36',NULL,NULL,'8554FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1448,2966,'Lice of the genus Pediculus, family Pediculidae. Pediculus humanus corporus is the human body louse and Pediculus humanus capitis is the human head louse.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:36',NULL,NULL,'11341FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1449,2967,'Personal history of sickle cell disease but not trait alone','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:36',NULL,NULL,'1468FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1450,2969,'Pathologic partial or complete loss of the ability to recall past experiences (AMNESIA, RETROGRADE) or to form new memories (AMNESIA, ANTEROGRADE). This condition may be of organic or psychologic origin. Organic forms of amnesia are usually associated with dysfunction of the DIENCEPHALON or HIPPOCAMPUS. (From Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, pp426-7)','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:36',NULL,NULL,'8537FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1451,2971,'Physiological disturbances in normal sexual performance.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:36',NULL,NULL,'7925FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1452,2973,'Sensation of discomfort, distress, or agony in the abdominal region.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:36',NULL,NULL,'12338FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1453,2975,'A papular eruption of unknown etiology that progresses to residual papular erythema and scaling usually confined to the area of the mouth, and almost exclusively occurring in young women. It may also be localized or extend to involve the eyelids and adjacent glabella area of the forehead (periocular dermatitis). (Dorland, 28th ed)','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:36',NULL,NULL,'9238FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1454,2977,'Loss of or impaired ability to smell. This may be caused by OLFACTORY NERVE DISEASES; PARANASAL SINUS DISEASES; viral RESPIRATORY TRACT INFECTIONS; CRANIOCEREBRAL TRAUMA; SMOKING; and other conditions.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:36',NULL,NULL,'10901FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1455,2978,'A gland in males that surrounds the neck of the BLADDER and the URETHRA. It secretes a substance that liquifies coagulated semen. It is situated in the pelvic cavity behind the lower part of the PUBIC SYMPHYSIS, above the deep layer of the triangular ligament, and rests upon the RECTUM.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:36',NULL,NULL,'9933FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1456,2979,'Significant weight loss in previous 30 days.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:36',NULL,NULL,'15903FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1457,2980,'A common nonarticular rheumatic syndrome characterized by myalgia and multiple points of focal muscle tenderness to palpation (trigger points). Muscle pain is typically aggravated by inactivity or exposure to cold. This condition is often associated with general symptoms, such as sleep disturbances, fatigue, stiffness, HEADACHES, and occasionally DEPRESSION. There is significant overlap between fibromyalgia and the chronic fatigue syndrome (FATIGUE SYNDROME, CHRONIC). Fibromyalgia may arise as a primary or secondary disease process. It is most frequent in females aged 20 to 50 years. (From Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, p1494-95)','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:36',NULL,NULL,'9891FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1458,2982,'A potentially fatal syndrome associated primarily with the use of neuroleptic agents (see ANTIPSYCHOTIC AGENTS) which are in turn associated with dopaminergic receptor blockade (see RECEPTORS, DOPAMINE) in the BASAL GANGLIA and HYPOTHALAMUS, and sympathetic dysregulation. Clinical features include diffuse MUSCLE RIGIDITY; TREMOR; high FEVER; diaphoresis; labile blood pressure; cognitive dysfunction; and autonomic disturbances. Serum CPK level elevation and a leukocytosis may also be present. (From Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, p1199; Psychiatr Serv 1998 Sep;49(9):1163-72)','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:36',NULL,NULL,'9870FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1459,2983,'Pleasure derived from being physically or psychologically abused, whether inflicted by oneself or by others. Masochism includes sexual masochism.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:37',NULL,NULL,'7924FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1460,2984,'Conditions which feature clinical manifestations resembling primary Parkinson disease that are caused by a known or suspected condition. Examples include parkinsonism caused by vascular injury, drugs, trauma, toxin exposure, neoplasms, infections and degenerative or hereditary conditions. Clinical features may include bradykinesia, rigidity, parkinsonian gait, and masked facies. In general, tremor is less prominent in secondary parkinsonism than in the primary form. (From Joynt, Clinical Neurology, 1998, Ch38, pp39-42)','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:37',NULL,NULL,'9869FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1461,2985,'Disorders in which anxiety (persistent feelings of apprehension, tension, or uneasiness) is the predominant disturbance.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:37',NULL,NULL,'12337FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1462,2987,'Excessive amount of watery fluid accumulated in the intercellular spaces, most commonly present in subcutaneous tissue.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:37',NULL,NULL,'9236FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1464,2991,'Sleep hyperhidrosis, more commonly known as the night sweats, is the occurrence of excessive sweating (hyperhidrosis) during sleep. The sufferer may or may not also suffer from excessive perspiration while awake. Sleep hyperhidrosis may occur at any age, but is most commonly seen in early adulthood.\r\nref: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night_sweats','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:37',NULL,NULL,'9837FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1465,2992,'A rash which produces a clear fluid as compared to a rash with pustular fluid.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:37',NULL,NULL,'15895FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1466,2993,'An abscess in the peritonsillar tissue extending into the tonsil capsule, resulting from suppuration of the tonsil. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:37',NULL,NULL,'9225FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1467,2994,'Pain in thoracic spine not caused by intervertebral disk disease.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:37',NULL,NULL,'17287FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1468,2995,'A condition in which there is a derivation of pleasure from inflicting pain, discomfort or humiliation on another person or persons. The sexual significance of sadistic wishes or behavior may be conscious or unconscious.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:37',NULL,NULL,'7922FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1469,2997,'Anxiety disorders in which the essential feature is persistent and irrational fear of a specific object, activity, or situation that the individual feels compelled to avoid. The individual recognizes the fear as excessive or unreasonable.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:37',NULL,NULL,'12328FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1470,2999,'Complete loss of phonation due to organic disease of the larynx or to nonorganic (i.e., psychogenic) causes.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:37',NULL,NULL,'10897FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1471,3000,'Sexually transmitted form of anogenital warty growth caused by the human papillomaviruses.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:37',NULL,NULL,'12321FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1472,3003,'Involuntary discharge of urine after the age at which urinary control should have been achieved; often used alone with specific reference to involuntary discharge of urine occurring during sleep at night (bed-wetting; nocturnal enuresis). (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:37',NULL,NULL,'9789FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1473,3004,'Inflammatory disease of the breast, or mammary gland.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:37',NULL,NULL,'11330FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1474,3006,'A syndrome of persistent pulmonary hypertension in the newborn infant, without demonstrable cardiac disease. It is characterized by cyanosis and acidosis, severe pulmonary vasoconstriction, hypertrophy of pulmonary arterial muscle, and elevated pulmonary vascular resistance, with resultant right-to-left shunting of blood through a patent ductus arteriosus and at times a patent foramen ovale.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:37',NULL,NULL,'9219FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1475,3009,'The forcible expulsion of the contents of the stomach through the mouth.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:37',NULL,NULL,'9208FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1476,3014,'Disorders characterized by recurrent TICS that may interfere with speech and other activities. Tics are sudden, rapid, nonrhythmic, stereotyped motor movements or vocalizations which may be exacerbated by stress and are generally attenuated during absorbing activities. Tic disorders are distinguished from conditions which feature other types of abnormal movements that may accompany general medical conditions. (From DSM-IV, 1994)','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:37',NULL,NULL,'12295FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1477,3016,'An exfoliative disease of skin seen primarily in adults and characterized by flaccid bullae and spreading erythema so that the skin has the appearance of being scalded. It results primarily from a toxic reaction to various drugs, but occasionally occurs as a result of infection, neoplastic conditions, or other exposure.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:37',NULL,NULL,'10867FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1478,3017,'Benign granulomatous disease of unknown etiology characterized by a ring of localized or disseminated papules or nodules on the skin and palisading histiocytes surrounding necrobiotic tissue resulting from altered collagen structures.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:37',NULL,NULL,'12205FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1479,3018,'Excessive lateral nail growth into the nail fold. Because the lateral margin of the nail acts as a foreign body, inflammation and granulation may result. It is caused by improperly fitting shoes and by improper trimming of the nail.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:37',NULL,NULL,'11322FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1480,3019,'Abnormally enlarged lymph nodes.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:37',NULL,NULL,'16216FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1481,3020,'A condition in which one or more of the arches of the foot have flattened out.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:37',NULL,NULL,'9206FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1482,3022,'Purplish or brownish red discoloration, easily visible through the epidermis, caused by hemorrhage into the tissues.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:37',NULL,NULL,'9205FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1483,3028,'Hyperthyroidism associated with a diffuse hyperplastic goiter resulting from production of an antibody directed against the thyroid-stimulating hormone (TSH) receptor, which acts as an agonist of TSH. (Braverman, The Thyroid, 6th ed, p648)','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:37',NULL,NULL,'12200FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1484,3031,'Disturbances in sexual desire and the psychophysiologic changes that characterize the sexual response cycle and cause marked distress and interpersonal difficulty. (APA, DSM-IV, 1994)','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:37',NULL,NULL,'11312FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1485,3032,'An acute inflammatory autoimmune neuritis caused by T cell- mediated cellular immune response directed towards peripheral myelin. Demyelination occurs in peripheral nerves and nerve roots. The process is often preceded by a viral or bacterial infection, surgery, immunization, lymphoma, or exposure to toxins. Common clinical manifestations include progressive weakness, loss of sensation, and loss of deep tendon reflexes. Weakness of respiratory muscles and autonomic dysfunction may occur. (From Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, pp1312-1314)','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:37',NULL,NULL,'12192FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1486,3034,'A benign tumor representing a congenital malformation of the lymphatic system and made up of newly formed lymph-containing vascular spaces and channels. Lymphangioendothelioma is a type of lymphangioma in which endothelial cells are the dominant component. (From Dorland, 27th ed)','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:37',NULL,NULL,'10861FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1487,3035,'A break, rupture, or crack, especially in bone or cartilage.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:37',NULL,NULL,'177FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1488,3036,'Perception of painful and nonpainful phantom sensations that occur following the complete or partial loss of a limb. The majority of individuals with an amputated extremity will experience the impression that the limb is still present, and in many cases, painful. (From Neurol Clin 1998 Nov;16(4):919-36; Brain 1998 Sep;121(Pt 9):1603-30)','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:37',NULL,NULL,'9203FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1489,3040,'A form of bronchial disorder associated with airway obstruction, marked by recurrent attacks of paroxysmal dyspnea, with wheezing due to spasmodic contraction of the bronchi.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:37',NULL,NULL,'12181FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1490,3042,'Edema due to obstruction of lymph vessels or disorders of the lymph nodes.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:38',NULL,NULL,'10856FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1491,3043,'A past medical history of malaria.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:38',NULL,NULL,'12179FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1492,3046,'The affective response to an actual current external danger which subsides with the elimination of the threatening condition.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:38',NULL,NULL,'9194FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1493,3047,'Subjectively experienced sensations in the absence of an appropriate stimulus, but which are regarded by the individual as real. They may be of organic origin or associated with MENTAL DISORDERS.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:38',NULL,NULL,'12162FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
(1494,3048,'Diseases of the urinary tract in both male and female. It does not include the male genitalia for which UROGENITAL DISEASES is used for general discussions of diseases of both the urinary tract and the genitalia.','en',2,'2025-12-19 08:40:38',NULL,NULL,'11305FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),
